    "function": "Involved in cell wall lipids remodeling and in virulence. Restricts the biofilm growth and is essential for the optimal intracellular survival of M.tuberculosis. Shows esterase activity with a preference for short-chain esters, particularly pNP-acetate (C2) and pNP-butyrate (C4). Has weaker activity with pNP-octanoate (C8), pNP-laurate (C12) and pNP-myristate (C14). Shows weak long-chain triacylglycerol (TAG) hydrolase activity in vitro. Not necessary for PPE17 stability or for its localization on the mycobacterial surface",
